    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161">

                <pb facs="0259" n="155" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/1288.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                            Germany to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-11T10:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 11, 1913—10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>German Government quite satisfied with Chinese proposal, but they have expressed
                    willingness to accept French counter-proposal. Will advise further as soon as
                    reply to German proposal is received.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leishman</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
